; Leg HD -- THE FLOW-CONTROL LEG (--rtscts).  Host SENDS and can now STOP.
;
; BENCH take-file: there is no "set line" here.  ~/.kermrc names the adapter.
; CHECK THAT IT NAMES THE ONE THAT IS PLUGGED IN.
;
; SET FLOW RTS/CTS ON THIS END.  It is meaningless without POSIX_CRTSCTS in
; SHOW FEATURES -- check before, not after.
;
; PUT THE ANALYZER ON THIS LEG.  Probe /RTS and /DTR on the TTL side (same
; WR5 byte, bit 7 and bit 1, so DTR is a free second channel); the connector
; is +/-12 V, do not probe there.  Add CTS if a channel is free -- SS16v's
; cts = 1 is on the retraction line because a floating MC1489 input can read
; active.  SS16an saw eight pauses of 785 ms-1 s with data STILL ARRIVING for
; hundreds of ms after each drop; that is the signature to compare against.
;
; THE RESULT IS rxpeak, and only if HD is otherwise identical to HC on the
; wire: rxbytes equal, same packet count, same retransmissions.  A leg that
; retransmits differently is re-run, not adjusted (SS16ag leg AM).
;
; THEN ASK WHERE THE PEAK IS BEFORE READING IT (SS16ak leg DE):
;     python3 v9k/tools/mapoffset.py s16bcHD.pkt \
;            --rxbytes <rxbytes= from the .OUT> <peakat= from the .OUT>
; A peak at a packet boundary is where the CONTROL legs peak too.
;
; V9K_FLOW stays FLO_NONE out of this sitting whatever this says.  Harmless
; and effective are different claims and only the second licenses a default.
;
; READ IT WITH:
;     python3 v9k/tools/pktstat.py --rxbytes <from STEPHD.OUT> s16bcHD.pkt
; Residual -11 clean, +28 with a startup timeout.
; cmp FIRST, then the counters.  A leg that is fast and wrong is the failure.

set flow rts/cts
set speed 38400
set receive timeout 20
set parity none
set prefixing cautious
set block 3
set retry 30
log packets s16bcHD.pkt
send rcvhd.dat
statistics
